              “degree” of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %em not
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+continuous+function"} degree of a continuous function
              (see there) in the usual sense of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheArchetypicalExample"}
          %p
          #NotionsOfRationalMaps.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (“rational maps”)
              %br/
              It it tradition (starting with Segal) to speak of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+maps"} rational maps
              in the following, but in the end the focus on
              %em regular rational maps
              (“morphisms”: e.g.
