            %p
          %p
            This is due to
            %a{:href => "#Segal79"} Segal 1979, Prop. 1.2, 1.3
            (bewaring the Note on terminology on p. 44). The analogous statement for rational curves in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+projective+spaces"} real projective spaces
            is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Mostovoy01"} Mostovoy 01
          %p
          #TheArchetypicalExample.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (the archetypical case)
              %br/
              In the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = S^2
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
              with its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SegalOnHomotopyTypeOfRationalMapsIntoCPn"}
              says that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
