            %p
              is an isomorphism on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              up to degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq d
          (
          %a{:href => "#Segal79"}> Segal 1979, Prop. 1.1’
          )
          %p
          #RelationToYangMillsMonopoles.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (relation to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopoles"} Yang-Mills monopoles
              %br/
              Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheArchetypicalExample"}
              controls the classification of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopoles"} Yang-Mills monopoles
          %p
          #RelationToGromovWittenTheory.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (relation to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+theory"} Gromov-Witten theory
              A compactification and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"} quotient stack
              of the space of rational maps in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RationalMappingSpaceInsideContinuousMappingSpace"} (2)
              is considered in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+theory"} Gromov-Witten theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Gromov-Witten+theory#Bertram02"} Bertram 2002, p. 9
          %p
          #RelationToTwistorStringTheory.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (relation to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
              %br/
              In the context of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to \mathbb{C}P^3
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RationalMappingSpaceInsideContinuousMappingSpace"} (2)
              are interpreted as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-brane"} D1-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+space"} twistor space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+3-space"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^3
              (
              %a{:href => "twistor+string+theory#Witten04"}> Witten 2004, Sec. 3
              ).
            %p
              Such rational maps are also argued to encode
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D8+supergravity"} D=4 N=8 supergravity
              (
              %a{:href => "twistor+string+theory#CachazoSkinner12"}> Cachazo &amp; Skinner 2012
              ,
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "twistor+string+theory#Adamo15"} Adamo 2015
            %p
              Here the number of poles in the rational function is the number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              of particles in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+function"} n-point function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/helicity"} helicity
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+order"} loop order
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} scattering amplitude
          %p
